ames></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Schiellerup</surname> <given-names>P</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Engberg</surname> <given-names>J</given-names></string-name>, <etal/><article-title>Virulence factors for hemolytic uremic syndrome, Denmark.</article-title><source>Emerg Infect Dis</source> <year>2004</year>;<volume>10</volume>:<fpage>842</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15200817</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R11"><label>11. </label><citation citation-type="journal"><string-name><surname>Prager</surname> <given-names>R</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Annemuller</surname> <given-names>S</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Tschape</surname> <given-names>H</given-names></string-name> <article-title>Diversity of virulence patterns among shiga toxin-producing <italic>Escherichia coli</italic> from human clinical cases-need for more detailed diagnostics.</article-title><source>Int J Med Microbiol</source> <year>2005</year>;<volume>295</volume>:<fpage>29</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>38</lpage> <pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.ijmm.2004.12.009</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15861814</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R12"><label>12. </label><citation citation-type="book"><collab>Centers for Disease Control and Prevention</collab> Foodborne Diseases Active Surveillance Network (FoodNet): population survey atlas of exposures, 2002. Atlanta: The Centers; <year>2004</year></citation></ref><ref id="R13"><label>13. </label><citation citation-type="other"><collab>California Food Emergency Response Team</collab> Investigation of an <italic>Escherichia coli</italic> O157:H7 outbreak associated with Dole pre-packaged spinach. Sacramento (CA): California Department of Health Services, US Food and Drug Administration; <year>2007</year></citation></ref><ref id="R14"><label>14. </label><citation citation-type="web"><string-name><surname>Brackett</surname> <given-names>RE</given-names></string-na